  "response": "**VERDICT: REVISE**\n\n**Overall Assessment**: The carousel implements a functional visual slider but lacks the programmatic state communication and landmark structure required by the WAI-ARIA APG Carousel pattern. Screen reader users will not know when slides change, active indicators won't be announced programmatically, and the component lacks a labeled region for context. The native `<button>` elements are correctly used, but the dynamic update pattern is incomplete.\n\n**Pre-commitment Predictions**:\nBefore reading code, I predicted:\n1. Missing `aria-live` region for announcing slide changes (dynamic content)\n2. Missing `role=\"region\"` / `aria-label` on the carousel container\n3. Active indicator state not communicated to AT (missing `aria-current`)\n4. No arrow key navigation per APG pattern\n5. Generic alt text fallback acceptable but potentially insufficient\n\nActual findings align with predictions. All predicted gaps are confirmed in code.\n\n**Critical Findings** (blocks access):\nNone. The component does not completely block access; keyboard users can navigate buttons, and images have `alt` attributes. However, dynamic state communication failures significantly degrade assistive technology usability.\n\n**Major Findings** (significantly degrades experience):\n1. **Missing `aria-live` region for slide announcements**\n   - Evidence: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:14-36` (carousel container and image swap logic)\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 4.1.3 (Status Messages), WAI-ARIA APG Carousel pattern requires a live region to announce slide changes\n   - Fix: Wrap the `<img>` or add a sibling `<div aria-live=\"polite\" role=\"status\">` that updates with `aria-label={`Image ${currentIndex + 1} of ${images.length}`} on index change.\n\n2. **Missing landmark/region labeling for the carousel**\n   - Evidence: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:14` (`<div className=\"carousel\">`)\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users, keyboard users navigating landmarks\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WAI-ARIA APG Carousel pattern requires `role=\"region\"` or `<section>` with `aria-label=\"Image carousel\"` (or similar) to provide context\n   - Fix: Change `<div className=\"carousel\">` to `<section className=\"carousel\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Image carousel\">`\n\n3. **Active indicator state not communicated to assistive technology**\n   - Evidence: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:27-33` (indicator buttons)\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users, low vision users relying on programmatic focus context\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value), WAI-ARIA APG Carousel pattern requires `aria-current=\"true\"` on the active indicator\n   - Fix: Add `aria-current={idx === currentIndex ? \"page\" : undefined}` to the indicator button. Remove reliance on `.active` CSS class for AT context.\n\n**Minor Findings** (friction but workaround exists):\n- **Missing arrow key navigation**: Per APG Carousel pattern, composite widgets should support arrow keys for slide navigation. Currently only buttons are available. Fix: Add `onKeyDown` handler to the carousel container or buttons to map `ArrowLeft`/`ArrowRight` to `goToPrevious`/`goToNext`.\n- **Generic alt text fallback**: `alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`} (line 17) works as a programmatic placeholder but provides no semantic value if images contain meaningful content. Fix: Pass descriptive `alt` strings via props or extract them from the `images` array structure.\n\n**Enhancements** (best practice not met):\n- Consider adding `aria-roledescription=\"slide\"` to the image container per APG recommendations for better screen reader context.\n- Add `tabIndex={0}` to the active indicator if you want it to receive focus automatically when slides change (optional, but improves flow).\n\n**What's Missing** (gaps, unhandled edge cases, unstated assumptions):\n- **Missing live region**: No mechanism announces dynamic content updates to AT. Screen reader users hear nothing when clicking \"Next\".\n- **Missing region context**: The carousel is a `<div>` with no landmark or label. Screen readers cannot identify it as a distinct interactive component.\n- **Missing programmatic active state**: Indicators rely solely on CSS classes. AT has no way to distinguish the current slide from others.\n- **Missing keyboard navigation model**: APG recommends arrow key support for carousels. Without it, users must tab through every button, which becomes tedious with many slides.\n\n**Multi-Perspective Notes**:\n- **Screen reader user**: Hears \"Previous image, button\", \"Next image, button\", and indicator numbers 1-N. Clicking \"Next\" changes the image visually but announces nothing. The component lacks a labeled region, so context is lost. Active indicator state is invisible to AT.\n- **Keyboard-only user**: Can tab to buttons and activate them with Enter/Space. Focus remains on the clicked button (acceptable per WCAG 2.4.3). No arrow key navigation means linear tabbing through all indicators if there are many slides.\n- **Low vision user (200% zoom, high contrast)**: Buttons contain text labels, indicators show numbers. Contrast and touch target sizes depend on CSS (not provided). Active state is visual-only; programmatic `aria-current` would help AT-based magnifiers or screen readers highlight the active element.\n- **Cognitive accessibility**: Labels are clear (\"Previous\", \"Next\", indicator numbers). Generic alt text may confuse users if images have specific meanings. No confirmation or timeout risks. Consistent button behavior.\n\n**Verdict Justification**: The component passes basic automated checks (native buttons, `alt` attributes present) but fails the WAI-ARIA APG Carousel pattern in three critical areas: dynamic state announcement (`aria-live`), landmark context (`role=\"region\"` + `aria-label`), and programmatic active state (`aria-current`). These are not preference issues; they are required for screen reader users to understand that content changed, what component they're interacting with, and which slide is active. The design must be revised before shipping.\n\n**Open Questions (unscored)**:\n- Do the `images` array items contain descriptive metadata that should be passed as `alt` text instead of the generic fallback?\n- Is arrow key navigation required by product specs, or are buttons sufficient for this carousel's slide count?\n- Are there any CSS transitions/animations on the image swap that might trigger `prefers-reduced-motion` concerns? (Not visible in code snippet)\n\n*Note on Phase 0*: No automated test evidence was provided. Findings are based on structural and pattern analysis per WAI-ARIA APG and WCAG 2.2. DOM verification of `aria-live` updates and `aria-current` application is recommended before final implementation to ensure framework re-render timing doesn't drop attributes.*",
